<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         REPAIR of a LIVE schema drift, measured on kind-dcre-dev 2026-09-11.

         MRG died at startup on a column this changelog says it creates:

           Caused by: org.postgresql.util.PSQLException:
             ERROR: column "man_report.type" does not exist

         The changelog is right and the database is stale. 2026/07/003-man-reporting.xml
         declares the column as `type`, ManReportEntity maps `type`, and the test suite
         expects `type`. The live table carries `report_type`. Measured live column list:

           dcre_man.man_report:
             id, client, report_type, trigger_kind, window_key, file_name, job_name,
             created_at

         WHY THE MIGRATION REPORTED SUCCESS WHILE THE SCHEMA WAS WRONG. The
         003-man-report changeset gained a re-run guard,
         onFail="MARK_RAN" over not/tableExists man_report, after that table already
         stood in its PRE-RENAME shape. A tableExists guard asks whether the NAME is
         taken; it cannot ask whether the SHAPE matches. So on a database holding the
         old table the createTable was recorded as applied WITHOUT running: a loud
         "relation already exists" became a silent wrong schema. Liquibase exited
         green, the history row now claims the create ran, and nothing will ever
         revisit it. That is what makes the drift permanent rather than transient, and
         it is why the repair has to be a separate changeset rather than an edit to
         the create.

         The changeset below converges the two reachable states and is the only thing
         that distinguishes them:

           stale database: report_type is present, the precondition PASSES, the
                           rename RUNS, and the column becomes type.
           fresh database: the column was created as type, the precondition FAILS,
                           and MARK_RAN records the changeset as applied without
                           running it.

         The fresh case is therefore a SECOND expected MARK_RAN on a database with no
         other writer, and ManV1BaselineIT names it rather than pattern-matching it,
         so a future conditional changeset still cannot join that exemption silently.

         Verified on this cluster: CockroachDB accepts
         ALTER TABLE x RENAME COLUMN a TO b.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <changeSet id="mrg-v2-report-type-rename" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <columnExists tableName="man_report" columnName="report_type"/>
        </preConditions>
        <renameColumn tableName="man_report" oldColumnName="report_type" newColumnName="type"/>
        <rollback>
            <renameColumn tableName="man_report" oldColumnName="type" newColumnName="report_type"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
